#CHLOEAI:1
TYPE="drift_log"
SCOPE="cross-cutting (fleet-level code/substrate drift journal)"
LOCATION="~/<your-workspace>/.repo-manager/drift_log.chloeai"
COMPANION_SKILL="~/<your-workspace>/.claude/skills/drift-sweep/"
RELATED_LOGS="~/.claude/skills/hi-mode/ski_lift_log.chloeai (tooling adoption — different concern)"

PURPOSE:
Append-only journal of code/substrate drift findings, tooling rollout actions,
and accepted-debt decisions across the repo fleet. The mechanism that catches
drift (drift-sweep skill) lives at .claude/skills/drift-sweep/; this log is
where what-we-found and what-we-did persists.

REVIEW_CADENCE:
- Append a new entry after any cross-repo drift sweep, single-repo install,
  or significant cleanup.
- Surface Open entries at STRATEGIC zoom sessions.
- Do not prune Resolved entries — the historical signal (what kinds of drift
  recur, in which repos) is the point.

ENTRY_FORMAT:
### YYYY-MM-DD | [REPO or CROSS-CUTTING] | Short Title
**Type:** sweep | single-repo-finding | install | refactor | accepted-debt
**Scope:** what was checked or changed
**Findings:** FAIL/WARN counts + specifics (or "n/a" for non-audit entries)
**Actions:** what was done — commits, configs added, deferred items
**Status:** Open | Resolved (YYYY-MM-DD) | Accepted (reason)
**Notes:** anything that matters for future readers

---

